            <ArticleTitle>[The role of inhalation provocation tests in the diagnosis of occupational bronchial asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Light industry female workers suffering from bronchial asthma demonstrated significant pulmonary ventilation disorders of mixed type with prevalent bronchial obstruction. Those changes prove long-standing harm caused by occupational factors. Inhalation provocative tests point out leading role of industrial dust in increased bronchial reactivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
